# Allowlist for scripts/pre-push-check.sh's hard-fail checks #7 (internal
# hostname / private IPv4) and #8 (ackstorm email). D36 made both checks
# hard failures; this file is the narrow, explicit escape hatch for the
# handful of matches that are legitimate today, so a real leak still fails
# the push.
#
# Format: one "<check>:<path>" pair per line, path relative to repo root,
# matched against the WHOLE path of the file the hit was found in (exact
# match, not a substring/glob). <check> is one of: hostname, privip, email.
# Every entry needs the one-line reason in a comment above it — this file
# is reviewed, not rubber-stamped.

# privip: devcontainer bootstrap creates a local docker bridge network for
# `kind` — a private subnet by definition, not a real internal host.
